  "description": "Conversion of existing offices to 6no. self-contained flats with associated waste/refuse and cycle store. Alterations to fenestrations (summary)",
  "site_name": "Development At Summit House 13",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "SCHEDULE OF CONDITIONS\n1) The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from \nthe date of this decision.\n2) The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with \ndrawing nos 12/24 04, 12/24 05, 12/24 06, 12/24 08, 12/24 09, 12/24 10, \n12/24 11, Site Plan 1:500 and Location Plan 1:1250. \n3) Before the development hereby permitted is first occupied, secure cycle \nstorage facilities shall be provided in accordance with details which have \nfirst been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning \nauthority. The secure cycle storage facilities shall be made available for use \nby occupiers of the proposed development and retained thereafter.\n4) The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until the basement\nStore window, ground floor Shop window, first floor kitchen/diner and \nbathroom windows serving Apartment 2 and second floor kitchen and \nbathroom windows serving Apartment 6 (as labelled on drawing nos 12/24 \n04, 12/24 05 and 12/24 06) on the north-eastern courtyard facing elevation \nhave been fitted with obscured glazing, and no part of those windows that \nare less than 1.7 metres above the floor of the room in which it is installed \nshall be capable of being opened. Details of the type of obscured glazing \nshall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority \nbefore the windows are installed and once installed the obscured glazing \nshall be retained thereafter.\n5) The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until all external \nwall surfaces within the courtyard area are finished with 3 no. coats of Dulux \nWeathershield Smooth Masonry Paint in Brilliant White or equivalent as \nagreed with the local planning authority, in accordance with the annotations \nshown on drawing nos 12/24 04, 12/24 05 and 12/24 06. The painted \nexternal wall surfaces shall be maintained and retained as such thereafter. \n6) All non-Combined Heat and Power gas fired boilers installed in this \ndevelopment must achieve dry NOx emission levels no greater than 40 \nmg/kWh.\n7) The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until the Building \nRegulations optional requirement of a water consumption rate of no more than \n110 litres per person per day has been complied with"
  ],
